    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But I don't want to be \"messy.\" I don't think I even know how to be anything else. To everyone else, I'm just the person who failed. When they look at me, they don't see someone \"finding themselves,\" they just see a disappointment. It’s like my whole life was a masterpiece and I just ruined the entire thing with one mistake. Everything is just... ruined. There’s no coming back from this.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea that you have to be a masterpiece is a lie you told yourself, and it's time to let that illusion shatter. Being \"messy\" is just another word for being human, and humans are inherently flawed, which is where the real strength lies. Don't try to fix the masterpiece; just accept that the canvas is blank, and that emptiness is actually a chance to finally choose what you want to paint next.",
      "source": "target",
